<code>assert element != null => element.equals(this.peek());</code>

Explanation:
- The comment specifies that if the element is not null, it should be equal to the last element in the queue after the operation.
- Since `peek()` returns the head of the queue, and the queue is circular, the last element added (if not null) will be the one at the head after an `offer` operation when the queue is full and wraps around.
- Therefore, we use `element.equals(this.peek())` to check if the last added element is equal to the head of the queue.
